WEBVTT

00:25:58.992 --> 00:26:00.805
But then post-IPO,

00:26:00.829 --> 00:26:03.845
those start-ups that were strong
cultures of commitment,

00:26:03.869 --> 00:26:05.298
they grew at slower rates,

00:26:05.322 --> 00:26:08.522
if you track metrics like
annual market capitalization.

00:26:08.546 --> 00:26:11.633
And I think that's where you start
to see some of the rigidity

00:26:11.657 --> 00:26:13.504
and groupthink problems come in,

00:26:13.528 --> 00:26:15.870
where you begin to weed out
diversity of thought,

00:26:15.894 --> 00:26:17.828
you end up with more homogeneity.

00:26:17.852 --> 00:26:20.451
And I guess where that's left me

00:26:20.475 --> 00:26:24.300
is wondering whether the kind
of charisma and conviction

00:26:24.324 --> 00:26:25.805
that you are describing in Adam

00:26:25.829 --> 00:26:29.495
is helpful for a company to grow
at an exorbitant rate early,

00:26:29.519 --> 00:26:32.458
and then over time, sort of,
shoots the company in the foot?